  "result": "`satisfies(version, range)` is now implemented in `src/semver.js` as `docs/SPEC.md` describes, and `npm test` passes (7 of 7).\n\nThe new tests are in `test/satisfies.test.js`. They cover:\n- matching and non-matching versions;\n- invalid input, which returns `false` without throwing;\n- prerelease ordering;\n- very large version numbers.\n\n- **Invalid sets:** an invalid comparator set makes the whole range invalid, so `1.2.3 || nope` returns `false` even though the first set matches.\n- **Operators and whitespace:** only `<`, `<=`, `>`, `>=` and `=` may be separated from their version by whitespace. `^ 1.2.3` counts as invalid, because the spec only allows the space for comparators.\n- **Prerelease rule:** a plain `<1.0.0` does not match `1.0.0-alpha`. The spec's prerelease rule requires a comparator with a prerelease on the same `MAJOR.MINOR.PATCH`, so this is intended.\n\nThe tests ran into two cases of my own mistakes, both in the tests rather than the implementation. I fixed them by correcting the test expectations.\n\nThe tool also reported that `test/satisfies.test.js` changed on disk after I last read it. I didn't re-read it, so I haven't looked at what changed.",
